# Email summary configuration for mobile-terminal-ops
# Copy to config/email-config and fill in your values (gitignored).
#
# Delivery method priority: local sendmail/mail > opt-in curl SMTP
#
# SECURITY MODEL
#   Live opencode output can contain findings, tokens, and secrets. By default
#   this project does NOT hand it to a third-party mail provider.
#   - Default path: your server's OWN mail relay (sendmail / local MTA). The
#     data stays on infrastructure you control.
#   - SMTP (Gmail, Outlook, ...): OPT-IN ONLY. Setting SMTP_URL/SMTP_USER/
#     SMTP_PASS is NOT enough — you must also set EMAIL_SMTP_OK="yes" to
#     confirm you understand a third party now sees (or transports) your
#     summaries. Even then, prefer EMAIL_ENCRYPT below.
#   - EMAIL_ENCRYPT: encrypt the full body so the provider only ever sees
#     ciphertext. Strongly recommended before you enable SMTP.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Your email address — every opencode response gets emailed here
EMAIL_TO=""

# ── Delivery ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Option 1 (DEFAULT): local relay. Works if your server can send mail
# via /usr/sbin/sendmail (postfix/exim) or the `mail` command.
#   Nothing extra to configure. For external delivery your MTA must relay.

# Option 2 (OPT-IN): SMTP via curl. Third-party providers see your summaries
# (or transport the encrypted payload). You must EXPLICITLY set:
EMAIL_SMTP_OK=""
#   SMTP_URL="smtps://smtp.gmail.com:465"
#   SMTP_USER="you@gmail.com"
#   SMTP_PASS="your16charapppassword"
#
#   Gmail requires 2FA + an app password:
#     1. https://myaccount.google.com/security → enable 2FA
#     2. https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords → generate one
#     3. Fill in below (app password WITHOUT spaces)
#
#   Outlook / Office 365:
#     SMTP_URL="smtp://smtp.office365.com:587"
#     SMTP_USER="you@outlook.com"
#     SMTP_PASS="your-password"
#
#   The script REFUSES to send via curl SMTP while EMAIL_SMTP_OK is empty.

# ── Encryption (strongly recommended if you use SMTP) ──
# Encrypts the full summary body so your provider can't read it.
# Choose one of:
#   EMAIL_ENCRYPT="none"   → plaintext body (local relay only, no SMTP)
#   EMAIL_ENCRYPT="gpg"    → GPG public-key encryption
#   EMAIL_ENCRYPT="age"    → age file encryption
#
# FAIL-CLOSED: if EMAIL_ENCRYPT is set but no encrypted payload can be
# produced (tool missing, recipient not in keyring), the script REFUSES to
# send rather than silently falling back to plaintext.
EMAIL_ENCRYPT="none"

# For gpg: a recipient whose public key is in your keyring. Decrypt on your
# phone with your private key, e.g.  gpg -d summary.gpg.asc
EMAIL_GPG_RECIPIENT=""

# For age: a recipient public key (age1...). Decrypt on your phone with:
#   age --decrypt --identity ~/.config/sops/age/keys.txt summary.age
EMAIL_AGE_PUBKEY=""

# ── Redaction (always on) ─────────────────────────────
# Email bodies are scrubbed of likely secrets before sending. Set to "no"
# only if you're sure the content contains nothing sensitive.
EMAIL_REDACT="yes"
# Extra custom patterns (one per line, extended regex) to also redact:
# EMAIL_REDACT_EXTRA=(
#   "my-secret-token-[a-z0-9]+"
# )

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────
EMAIL_FROM=""

# ── Watcher Defaults ─────────────────────────────────
# These can be overridden via CLI flags:
#   --poll N   --stall N   --cool N
POLL_INTERVAL=4
STALL_TIMEOUT=120
OUTPUT_COOLDOWN=15